{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778615627882,"sessionID":"ses_1e2468f05ffe6pzlCKze9keZSU","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"functions.write:22","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md","content":"## Summary\nRelabels **MONDO:0012277** from \"myofibrillar myopathy 4\" to \"LDB3-related myofibrillar myopathy\" per ClinGen Muscular Dystrophies and Myopathies GCEP request (issue #9938).\n\n## Changes Made\n1. ** Primary label updated **  \\\n   `name: myofibrillar myopathy 4` → `name: LDB3-related myofibrillar myopathy`\n\n2. ** Old label preserved as synonym **  \\\n   Added `synonym: \"myofibrillar myopathy 4\" EXACT [OMIM:609452]` to maintain discoverability and backward compatibility.\n\n## Rationale\nThe ClinGen GCEP prefers explicit gene-related disease names (e.g., `{GENE}-related {disease}`) over OMIM numerical suffixes. MONDO already follows this pattern for many disease-series-by-gene terms, and the term's logical definition uses `has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in LDB3`, making the new label consistent with its axiomatization. The existing exact synonym \"ZASP-related myofibrillar myopathy\" (LDB3's former symbol) further supports this relabeling.\n\n## Validation Performed\n- [x] Checked out term with `obo-checkout.pl`\n- [x] Edited in `terms/` directory per MONDO workflow\n- [x] Checked in with `obo-checkin.pl`\n- [x] Normalized serialization via `make NORM` (ODK docker)\n- [x] Syntax validated with `robot convert` (no errors)\n- [x] Verified diff: only the label and one synonym line changed\n\n## Source Attribution\n- Requester ORCID: `0000-0002-2078-7280`\n- ClinGen affiliation: `https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/`\n"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"PR_COMMENTS.md","time":{"sta